    <summary>One local MCP connection for KillerTools and the Killer app family.</summary>
    <description>KillerMCP gives MCP compatible agents one local connection to the KillerTools utilities and the Killer apps installed on the computer.

**Features:**

- All 81 KillerTools website utilities from the native KillerTools engine
- Automatic tool discovery for supported versions of KillerPDF, KillerScan, KillerNotes, KillerShell, Killendar, KillerBench, and KillerShot
- Registers itself with Codex, Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Gemini CLI, and Windsurf when they are found
- Labeled tool effects and a local tool call log that never records arguments or results
- Signed updates that must match the published SHA256 and pass Windows signature verification
- Installs for the current user and requires the .NET 10 Desktop Runtime
- GPLv3, local-only, no account, no telemetry
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SteveTheKiller/KillerMCP/releases/tag/vREPLACE_VERSION</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="dotnet-10.0-desktopruntime" version="[10.0.0,11.0.0)" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
